 "id": "break/client-edit-and-operator/hot/5m",
 "description": "The client edits message 3, inside the cached prefix, and cmdfilter shortens a new 8,000-token output (message 9) to 1,000 tokens. The client's last breakpoint before the edit is the end of message 2, so B* is the end of message 2: the provider reads 11,000 tokens and writes the rest, in the client's bill as well as in the forwarded one. The edit is on the record as a break with no ChangeID and moves no token, because the client body would have stopped reading at the same place. cmdfilter's 7,000 tokens are after B*, so they are writes: +7,000 x $3.75 = +$0.02625. The edit does not reduce or raise that figure.",
